  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A, B, C$ be three non-void subsets of set $S$. Let $(A \\cap C) \\cup\\left(B \\cap C^{\\prime}\\right)=\\phi$ where $C^{\\prime}$ denote the complement of set $C$ in S. Then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Htunl",
      "text": "$A \\cap B=\\phi$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "43nAt",
      "text": "$A \\cap B \\neq \\phi$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NK5Lf",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{A} \\cap \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{A}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hZVk2",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{A} \\cup \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{A}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$(A \\cap C) \\cup\\left(B \\cap C^{\\prime}\\right)=\\phi$\r\n$\\Rightarrow A \\cap C=\\phi$ and $B \\cap C^{\\prime}=\\phi$ ...(i)\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{B} \\subseteq \\mathrm{C}$ ...(ii)\r\nfrom (i) and (ii)\r\n$A \\cap B=\\phi$",
